1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
A dramatic wildlife shot is never worth putting an animal at risk.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Baiting can change where animals go and how they behave.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Follow local wildlife guidance.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Never lure animals toward people or roads.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Don't chase an animal, block its escape route,

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
or get closer just to fill the frame.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Use a longer lens and keep a safe, lawful distance.

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Let the animal decide what happens next.

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Record natural sound. Hold the shot.

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Give the moment room to unfold.

11
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Responsible wildlife filmmaking isn't about controlling nature.

12
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Protect the animal first.

13
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
The story comes second.
